This is the single biggest fix for reliable incremental builds on this
codebase, found while inspecting why retries appeared to start over.

release/src-rt/Makefile (symlinked as
release/src-rt-5.04axhnd.675x/Makefile) has two device-name pattern rules
that match "gt-ax6000"/"GT-AX6000" (`gt-% GT-%:` and a second explicit
model list). Both unconditionally do, on EVERY invocation of `make
gt-ax6000`, success or retry, changed or unchanged:

    rm -fr router-sysdep
    cp -ar router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B)/ router-sysdep

router-sysdep.gt-ax6000/ is 817 files / 32MB spanning ~90 components
(bcm_util, wlan, wlconf, wlcsm, ethctl, fcctl, bridge-utils, mtd, and
more) - and critically, router-sysdep (no suffix) is not just a source
copy, it's also where these components get COMPILED: object/library
outputs land inside router-sysdep/<component>/ alongside the copied
source. Deleting the whole tree before every build destroys every
previously-compiled output in it, forcing a full rebuild of this entire
subtree regardless of whether anything actually changed. Confirmed
directly against a real failing build log: bcm_ethswutils.o was compiling
inside router-sysdep/bcm_util/, which only exists via this copy step.

Fix: replace the unconditional wipe+copy with an incremental sync
(rsync -a --delete). This preserves Make's own native mtime-based
dependency tracking rather than requiring a separate invalidation system
for this component: rsync only touches files that actually changed
(so existing .o/.so outputs for unchanged sources are left alone and
correctly seen as up to date), while --delete still removes anything no
longer present in the source (so a file removed from
router-sysdep.gt-ax6000/ doesn't linger as stale content the way it would
with a plain incremental copy). rsync is already a build dependency
(firmware/docker/Dockerfile installs it).

Verified git apply --check and a full apply-then-revert cycle against
the pinned tag (3004.388.9) checkout, including confirming the fix lands
correctly at both occurrences.

diff --git a/release/src-rt/Makefile b/release/src-rt/Makefile
index 9792990eac..7ff9c10a53 100755
--- a/release/src-rt/Makefile
+++ b/release/src-rt/Makefile
@@ -6260,9 +6260,9 @@ endif
 
 ifeq ($(HND_ROUTER),y)
 ifeq ($(or $(HND_ROUTER_AX_675x),$(HND_ROUTER_AX)),y)
-	@echo "Copy router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B) content"
-	@rm -fr router-sysdep
-	@cp -ar router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B)/ router-sysdep
+	@echo "Sync router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B) content into router-sysdep (incremental)"
+	@mkdir -p router-sysdep
+	@rsync -a --delete router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B)/ router-sysdep/
 else	# RT-AC86U or GT-AC2900
 	@cp -ar $(TOP_PLATFORM)/hnd_extra/prebuilt/$(BUILD_NAME)/* $(TOP_PLATFORM)/hnd_extra/prebuilt/
 endif
@@ -6285,9 +6285,9 @@ ETJ etj:
 ET12 et12 XT12 xt12 XD4PRO xd4pro XT8PRO xt8pro BM68 bm68 XT8_V2 xt8_v2 ET8PRO et8pro ET8_V2 et8_v2 GT10 gt10 XD6_V2 xd6_v2 BR63 br63 BC109 bc109 BC105 bc105 EBG19 ebg19 EBG15 ebg15 XC5 xc5 eba63:
 	$(call save_src_config, $@,_CFG)
 ifeq ($(or $(HND_ROUTER_AX_675x),$(HND_ROUTER_AX)),y)
-	@echo "Copy router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B) content"
-	@rm -fr router-sysdep
-	@cp -ar router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B)/ router-sysdep
+	@echo "Sync router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B) content into router-sysdep (incremental)"
+	@mkdir -p router-sysdep
+	@rsync -a --delete router-sysdep.$(lowercase_B)/ router-sysdep/
 endif
 	$(MAKE) bin
 
